Behaviour & configuration schema
--------------------------------
The Alarmo websocket protocol, service payloads and the YAML configuration
surface were reimplemented from **alarmo-card** by **Niels Faber**
(https://github.com/nielsfaber/alarmo-card), licensed Apache-2.0.

No source code was copied. The upstream card was read as a functional
reference so that an existing `custom:alarmo-card` configuration keeps
working here with only the `type:` line changed. Where this card deliberately
diverges from upstream behaviour, the difference is recorded in
docs/MIGRATING.md.

Visual design system
--------------------
The layout tokens, colour formula, control geometry and animation timings
reproduce the design system of **lovelace-mushroom** by **Paul Bottein**
(https://github.com/piitaya/lovelace-mushroom), licensed Apache-2.0.

This is a closer form of borrowing than the above: CSS declarations in the
"Mushroom primitives" region of dist/alarmo-mushroom-card.js are faithful
reproductions of Mushroom's own, renamed into an `--amc-*` namespace and
re-expressed as classes rather than custom elements.

This card does not require, bundle, or modify lovelace-mushroom. It reads
`--mush-*` custom properties when they are present so that a Mushroom theme
already installed in Home Assistant themes this card too.

